<details class="vat-panel vat-help"><summary>How this is computed</summary><p>Regular corporate tax uses reviewed 20% / 25% eligibility, the year’s itemized / OSD election, and reviewed MCIT applicability. Unconfirmed or unsupported tax computations remain blank. Quarterly income, adjustments and explicitly allocated NOLCO accumulate; Annual is a full-year computation, not a sum of quarterly tax due. Posted income-tax 2307s are credits; VAT-withheld certificates are excluded. Only earlier-quarter tax payments become credits in later returns; penalties never do.</p><p>NOLCO defaults to the next three taxable years, or five for losses identified as taxable years 2020 or 2021. Eligibility, ownership requirements, fiscal-year identification and filed applications require review. Excess MCIT and special or individual tax regimes require separate reviewed treatment; this page does not silently apply them.</p><p><a href="https://bir-cdn.bir.gov.ph/local/pdf/1702Q%202018ENCS%20final2.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BIR 1702Q</a> · <a href="https://bir-cdn.bir.gov.ph/local/pdf/RR%20No.%2025-2020.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RR 25-2020 · NOLCO</a></p></details>
